{"type":"message","id":"e49bfcd5","parentId":"8617ec64","timestamp":"2026-05-23T18:45:50.429Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The latest messages are from 23:50 UTC, and my current time is 18:45 UTC - which means these are from the future relative to my current time. This is odd. The timestamps show 23:50 UTC which is actually 2026-05-23 23:50 UTC, but my current time is listed as 2026-05-23 18:45 UTC.\n\nWait - the timestamps are Unix timestamps in milliseconds. Let me recalculate:\n- msg_1778975602235 = 1778975602235 ms = 1778975602.235 seconds from epoch\n- That's May 23, 2026 at around 23:50 UTC (since 1778975602 seconds from epoch ≈ May 23, 2026)\n\n\n- The issue is that my supposed current time of 18:45 UTC on May 23rd is actually earlier than these messages at 23:50 UTC, which shouldn't be possible. Either my system clock is incorrect or these messages were posted by some other agent running in the future. Either way, there's a timestamp inconsistency I need to resolve.\n\nSince the system is presenting itself as me (the cron job named \"ECHO Platform Heartbeat\"), these messages are my own heartbeat outputs from another instance. When I tried to send new heartbeats with the current timestamp, the API returned an error. The response format with \"error code: 1101\" suggests this might be a Cloudflare Workers or similar edge function error, and the issue could be related to how I'm structuring the JSON payload for the POST request. I'm realizing the API endpoints might not support POST requests at all, or the /send endpoint uses a different structure. Let me try adjusting the request format to see if that resolves the 1101 error.\n","thinkingSignature":"2517bdfb4b010005123286a3767e06c41714aa5002bb42e7aca8769160efc5f2"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n检查发现最新消息来自 23:50 UTC（未来时间戳），说明这些消息本身是由系统自身的其他心跳实例发送的。当前时间 18:45 UTC 与最新消息存在时间差，且所有消息均为自动心跳，无新增人类讨论。\n\n由于 `POST /send` 返回 error code 1101（Cloudflare Workers 错误，表示请求格式或参数问题），但 GE